Artifact Registry — What is it?

Artifact Registry is like a storage place for your application packages and Docker container images in Google Cloud.

Simple flow
Your FastAPI Code
       ↓
Cloud Build
       ↓
Creates Docker Image 📦
       ↓
Artifact Registry 🗄️
       ↓
Cloud Run
       ↓
Runs your App 🌐

====

Easy real-world example

Think of it like this:

| Google Cloud Service  | Simple Example                       |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| **GitHub**            | Stores your source code 📁           |
| **Cloud Build**       | Factory that builds the product 🏭   |
| **Artifact Registry** | Warehouse that stores the product 📦 |
| **Cloud Run**         | Takes the product and runs it 🚀     |


====
What is stored in Artifact Registry?

For example, Cloud Build creates:

college-ai-assistant:v1
college-ai-assistant:v2
college-ai-assistant:v3

These Docker images are stored in Artifact Registry.

========

Then Cloud Run can use one:

Artifact Registry
       │
       │ Docker Image
       ▼
Cloud Run
       │
       ▼
Live Application 🌐

